---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  path="/subgraphs"
  title="Nest-backed subgraphs - Nuthatch"
  description="The Graph is sunsetting support for a number of chains. Nuthatch ports a subgraph that is no longer live on the network to a nest from the same contracts, and hosts it for you."
>
  <section class="page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="section-label">Subgraphs</p>
      <h1>Nest-backed subgraphs</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The Graph is sunsetting support for a number of chains, and subgraphs on them are going dark. We port a
        subgraph that is no longer live on the network to a nest from the same contracts. Its event-derived
        fields answer exactly; a field a mapping computes is refused by name, so check your app's queries against
        the port before switching. We build each port on request and run it on our servers, with no billing and
        no accounts.
      </p>

      <p class="empty">
        On request. Reach out on the <a href="https://discord.gg/p9Xc45txWa" rel="noopener">Nuthatch Discord</a>
        with the subgraph, or its contracts and chain.
      </p>

      <section class="chains">
        <h2>A chain The Graph does not serve</h2>
        <p>
          Nuthatch indexes any EVM chain that has a JSON-RPC endpoint, including chains The Graph network does not
          support or no longer supports. A set of chains is built in; for any other,
          <code>nuthatch init 0xYourContract --chain my-chain --rpc https://your-endpoint</code> reads the chain id
          from the endpoint and checks it at every start. <a href="/docs/reference/config/">The config reference</a>
          shows the same nest written by hand, and <a href="/docs/build/subgraph-fallback">the fallback docs</a> cover
          answering a subgraph's queries from it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Non-EVM chains such as NEAR or Solana are not built today; support is added on request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="notes">
        <section>
          <h2>Run it yourself</h2>
          <p>
            A hosted port is the stock <code>nuthatch-graph</code> download run as any operator would run it, so you
            can take it in-house whenever you like.
            <a href="https://github.com/nuthatch-org/nuthatch/blob/main/docs/stopgap/betswirl-bnb.md" rel="noopener">The BetSwirl BNB Chain port</a>
            shows how, and <a href="/the-graph">Nuthatch and The Graph</a> explains how it sits beside the network.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem) clamp(4rem, 9vw, 6.5rem); }
  h1 { margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
  .lede { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 2.2rem; max-width: 64ch; }
  .empty {
    border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.2rem 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.86rem; margin: 0;
  }
  .chains { margin-top: 2.5rem; max-width: 64ch; }
  .chains h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .chains p { color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 0.8rem; }
  .notes { margin-top: 3rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(18rem, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 2rem; }
  .notes h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .notes p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.93rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0; }
</style>
